{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01KGrPuNPJekz3XetDJPACNn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Summary of the `anchor_gui.py` deliverable, grounded in the member document:\n\n**What it is**\n- `anchor_gui.py` is a self-contained Python HTTP server (8,093 lines) that serves the interactive Anchor dashboard and exposes API endpoints; every UI action (done, add, capture) writes directly to the markdown files and logs the change (module docstring, lines 1â€“14).\n- It uses only the Python standard library â€” `json, logging, os, re, socket, sys, threading, time, traceback, webbrowser`, plus `http.server`, `urllib.parse`, and `html` (imports, lines 16â€“21).\n\n**Paths & data layout**\n- Data paths resolve through the shared `paths` helper, honoring the `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR` env var (unset â†’ the code dir). It binds the markdown sources: `DASHBOARD_MD`, `PROJECTS_MD`, `INBOX_MD`, `DOMAINS_DIR`, `LOGS_DIR`, `CANCELLED_MD`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER_MD` (lines 27â€“47).\n- Reflects the single-folder layout (consolidated 2026-05-02 from the prior dual-folder PSU + Axmra setup) (comment, lines 24â€“25).\n\n**Concurrency & logging**\n- A process-wide `WRITE_LOCK` (from `paths`) is held around every markdown/JSON mutation so concurrent mutating requests under `ThreadingHTTPServer` can't lose an update (lines 29â€“31; `_with_write_lock` decorator at line 3885).\n- Errors log to `logs/errors.log` via `logging`, with a guard against double-handler attach when imported more than once (e.g. by `anchor_healthcheck`) and `propagate=False` to avoid duplicated lines (lines 49â€“71).\n\n**Markdown parsing & data gathering**\n- Parsing helpers read markdown into Python dicts: `parse_tasks_from_md`, `parse_projects_from_md`, `parse_inbox_from_md`, `parse_archived_tasks` (lines 181â€“318); `gather_all()` aggregates dashboard + domain files (line 319).\n\n**Change operations**\n- Task lifecycle ops write back to markdown: `mark_done`, `mark_undone`, `add_task`, `capture_inbox`, `link_task`, `edit_task`, `edit_project`, `cancel_task`, `save_for_later`, `restore_task`, with `log_change` and archive append helpers (lines 3894â€“4318).\n\n**R&D control surface (v2â€“v4) rendering**\n- Renders the per-project window via `render_project_window_html` (lines 1856â€“3646) â€” by far the largest function â€” plus a Kanban (`_render_kanban_html`, 1618), lane tiles/session cards (`_render_lane_sessions`, 1693), a grass idea board (`_render_grass_board`, 1579), effort/cost rollups (`render_header_rollup_html` 1828, `render_cost_rollup_html` 3657), deliverables view (`render_deliverables_html`, 3785), and project tiles/rows (1106, 1208, 1226).\n- Triggers proactive, cached summaries in background threads: `_trigger_project_summary`, `_trigger_session_summary`, `_trigger_project_session_summaries` (lines 905â€“1022).\n\n**ConPTY terminal transport (v3/v4)**\n- Implements a hand-rolled RFC-6455 WebSocket codec in stdlib: `ws_accept_key`, `encode_text_frame`, `encode_close_frame`, `encode_pong_frame`, `decode_frames` (lines 463â€“632), serving PTY bytes via `_serve_term_ws` (6537) with token auth `_term_token_ok` (6424) and SSE fallbacks `_serve_term_sse`/`_serve_term_stream2` (6315, 6441).\n- Static-asset routes are traversal-guarded (`_unsafe_path_seg`, 634) for the vendored anchor-term, xterm, and brand assets (`anchor_term_asset`, `xterm_asset`, `brand_asset`, lines 659â€“750).\n\n**HTTP server**\n- `AnchorHandler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler)` (line 6270) routes `do_GET` (6677) and `do_POST` (7159); `generate_html` (4320) builds the full dashboard HTML with embedded CSS/JS in one string.\n- Single-instance enforcement: `_ExclusiveThreadingHTTPServer` overrides `server_bind` (lines 7941â€“7968) to bind exclusively (the `SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE` guard against a duplicate supervisor squatting 8777); `make_server` defaults to host `127.0.0.1`, port `8777` (7970), with `resolve_bind_host` (7999) and a `_heartbeat_watchdog` (7930).\n\n**Build identity / cache-busting**\n- Computes a build id once at startup (`_compute_build_id`, line 78) used by self-healing client JS (`cache_bust_script`, 144) to detect a redeploy and force a cache-busting reload."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":638,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4267,"cache_read_input_tokens":49260,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4267},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa3b1266-f77a-426c-b084-df8a986e21a3","uuid":"eff513b2-12b9-4628-acf7-5a17d5b6febb","request_id":"req_011Cc1JR4gNDovQ4ZWUKC4HA"}
